# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: StoryBeginnings | Scene: DayOfTheFuneral

translate es strings:

    old "The day of King Orwell's funeral has arrived."
    new "Ha llegado el día del funeral de Orwell, el rey."

    old "A week has passed since his body was found."
    new "Han pasado una semana desde que fue encontrado su cadáver."

    old "In attendance are all the great houses and families of Rosanna, come to pay their final respects."
    new "Asisten todas las grandes casas y familias de Rosanna, acudidas para rendirles su último homenaje."

    old "Beloved in life and beloved in death, a nation mourns the passing of their king."
    new "Amado en vida y amado en la muerte, una nación lamenta el paso de su rey."

    old "Sarah looks out over the crowd of people that have fitted themselves into the great hall."
    new "Sarah observa a la multitud de personas que se han acomodado en la gran sala."

    old "Sarah..."
    new "Sarah..."

    old "Thomas embraces his sister."
    new "Thomas abraza a su hermana."

    old "Who would have wanted to hurt Dad?"
    new "¿Quién querría hacer daño al papá?"

    old "Sarah can't find the will to hug him back."
    new "Sarah no encuentra el ánimo para corresponderlo con un abrazo."

    old "It's okay Thomas, we just need to get through today. Let those questions rest for another day."
    new "Está bien, Thomas, solo necesitamos superar el día de hoy. Dejemos esas preguntas para otro día."

    old "Then what?"
    new "¿Y después?"

    old "Thomas sounded exasperated."
    new "Thomas sonaba exasperado."

    old "Then another day. Coronation. Another day. On and on, Thomas. We just need to keep moving forward. Dad might not be here anymore, but he's watching over us."
    new "Otro día. Coronación. Otro día. Y así sigue, Thomas. Solo necesitamos seguir avanzando. Papá quizás ya no esté aquí, pero nos está vigilando."

    old "Sarah turns to her brother, looking deep into his eyes. His eyes are bloodshot from the crying that he hides from her."
    new "Sarah se gira hacia su hermano, mirando profundamente en sus ojos. Sus ojos están rojos por el llanto que le oculta."

    old "We need to make him proud now. Remember: composure."
    new "Necesitamos hacerlo sentir orgulloso ahora. Recuerda: compostura."

    old "Thomas turns away from her, staring off into the distance, trying to look at nothing at all."
    new "Thomas se aparta de ella, mirando al vacío, intentando no ver nada en absoluto."

    old "Sarah tries to remember the week since her father's death."
    new "Sarah intenta recordar la semana desde la muerte de su padre."

    old "She had to do so much, in a way, it spared her from dealing with her grief."
    new "Tenía que hacer tanto, de cierto modo, lo cual le ahorraba enfrentar su dolor."

    old "Invitations, decorations, preparations. An endless amount of work for her to lose herself in."
    new "Invitaciones, decoraciones, preparativos. Una cantidad interminable de trabajo para que ella se pierda en él."

    old "Thomas, on the other hand, had turned inwards. He had grown more somber, and she had found him on some nights, walking through the dark unlit castle halls."
    new "Thomas, por otro lado, se había vuelto hacia adentro. Había crecido más sombrío, y ella lo había encontrado algunas noches caminando por los oscuros pasillos del castillo sin luz."

    old "Sarah made a mental note, she needed to talk to her brother. It pained her to admit it, but he wasn't strong. He needed to know he could lean on her."
    new "Sarah tomó nota mental; necesitaba hablar con su hermano. Le dolía admitirlo, pero él no era fuerte. Necesitaba saber que podía apoyarse en ella."

    old "The events of the day proceeded. Priests read out the last rites. Some spoke words of comfort."
    new "Los acontecimientos del día transcurrieron. Los sacerdotes leyeron los últimos ritos. Algunos pronunciaron palabras de consuelo."

    old "Not before long, Sarah and Thomas found themselves in the middle of the great hall, walking in linked arms, floating from one group of nobles to the next."
    new "Poco después, Sarah y Thomas se encontraron en medio del gran salón, caminando de la mano mientras flotaban suavemente de un grupo de nobles a otro."

    old "Our condolences."
    new "Nuestras condolencias."

    old "He was a great man."
    new "Era un gran hombre."

    old "He will be missed."
    new "Se le echará de menos."

    old "Sarah didn't want to sound cynical, she was sure that many of them truly meant what they said. It just seemed like words, not just these words but all words, seemed so empty right now."
    new "Sarah no quería sonar cínica; estaba segura de que muchos de ellos realmente querían lo que decían. Pero todo parecía tan vacío ahora mismo, no solo estas palabras, sino todas las palabras."

    old "Soon, she found herself subjected to a torrent of sympathies. It all became too much."
    new "Pronto, se vio sumida en una marea de simpatías. Todo resultó demasiado."

    old "Thomas, I need to take a moment, please carry on without me."
    new "Thomas, necesito un momento, por favor continúa sin mí."

    old "Sarah unlinked her arm from her brother and quickly walked away."
    new "Sarah desvinculó su brazo de su hermano y se alejó rápidamente."

    old "Fresh air, that's what she needed."
    new "Aire fresco, eso es lo que necesitaba."
